{title: 506 - A Mighty Fortress}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: C}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Christian Life}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[Am]A mighty fortress [Em]is our God, [F]Abulwark never [C]failing;
[Am]Our helper [Dm]he amid the flood Of [G]mortal ills [C]prevailing.
[C]For still our ancient foe Doth seek to work us woe;
[G]His craft and power [Em]are [Am]great, And armed with [Dm]cruel hate,
[G]On earth is not his equal.

Verse 2:
[Am]Did we [Em]in our [F]own strength [C]confide,
[Am]our striving [Em]would [F]be losing,
[Am]were not [Dm]the right man [G]on our [C]side,
[C]the man of God's own choosing.
[C]Dost ask who that may be?
[C]Christ Jesus, it is he;
[G]Lord Sabbaoth, [Am]his name,
[G]from age to age the same,
[G]and he must win the battle.

Verse 3:
[Am]And though [Em]this world, [F]with devils [C]filled,
[Am]should threaten [Em]to [F]undo [C]us,
[Am]we will [Dm]not fear, for [G]God hath [C]willed
[C]his truth to triumph through us.
[C]The Prince of Darkness grim,
[C]we tremble not for him;
[G]his rage [Em]we [Am]can endure,
[G]for lo, his doom is sure;
[G]one little word shall fell him.

Verse 4:
[Am]That word above [Em]all [F]earthly [C]powers,
[Am]no thanks [Em]to them, [F]abideth;
[Am]the Spirit [Dm]and the [G]gifts are [C]ours,
[C]thru him who with us sideth.
[C]Let goods and kindred go,
[C]this mortal life also;
[G]the body [Am]they may [Dm]kill;
[G]God's truth abideth still;
[G]his kingdom is forever.
